   <title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title>
   <link>https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss</link>
   <description>Fears of xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</description>
